{
  "slug": "intern-101",
  "name": "Intern 101",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code plugin for working professionals, generally interns. Five skills that handle the repetitive parts of a work session: organizing a project directory, saving session context, picking up where you left off, and writing your daily update.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `catchup` (Use when the user starts a session and wants to know what they were working on, says \"what…), `chat-context-extractor` (Reads a Claude Code .jsonl session transcript and produces a structured, searchable markdown context document), `daily-update` (Use when the user wants to generate a daily status update for their supervisor, says \"write my daily…), `extract-today` (Use when the user wants to save all of today's Claude sessions as context documents, says \"extract today's…), `project-index-manager` (Use when a project directory has scattered files across multiple work domains with no clear organization, when starting…), `recall` (Use when the user wants to find past sessions related to a topic, asks \"did we work on…), `status` (Use when the user wants an overview of all sub-project statuses, asks \"what's the state of everything?\", \"show…)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install intern-101@claude-community` from `Arnav1906/intern-101`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
